A||||2||Shaun41178||Fiero beats Grand National
Z||000000||Shaun41178||09-04-99||12:46 AM||||I didn't feel like typing it all out again so I just copied what I had written on a camaro BB and am reposting it here.  I hope no one minds. <IMG SRC="/ubb/redface.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15>)<p>I went to Norwalk tonight for TNT and made 4 passes. One of the runs was against a Grand National, of what year I don't know but I remember looking under the hood earlier in the evening and that engine just looked awesome. It said "3.8 SFI Turbo" on the hood or "3.8 Turbo" on the hood one of the two if that helps to figure out what year it was.<br>There are 8 staging lanes so it is hard to tell who you will be going up against untill you are the next person to race. Well The car next to me happened to end up being a GN. I was pretty excited cause this was the best car that I had gone up against that evening. I had seen it run earlier in the evening and it ran a 14.5 so I knew I had my work cut out for me here.<p>So I roll around the water box and do a power brake to spin the tires real quick to get any big rubber off or water. I stage and he stages also. The light turns green and I beat him out of the hole with my lazy .801 to his 1.0 reaction time. Right after i leave the line and build a little rpms I hit the nitrous. I cranked off a 1.96 60'. The GN unfortunately spun bad out of the hole even with the highly sprayed track with a 2.4 60'. I kept checking my mirror to see if he was gaining but he wasn't. In fact I was pulling away ever so slightly. I couldn't believe that I was outrunning a GN! The 1/4 was appraoching quickly and I was praying that this guy wouldn't pull something out of his hat and come flying by me. I was able to hold on though for the victory. YES!! Went through the traps and picked up my timeslip. I ran a 14.488 to his 15.076. Now I don't know how many lengths that is but he was pretty visible in my rearview as i crossed the line. I guess it could be figured out but I would say about 5-6.<p>I was happy but sad at the same time for beating this GN as I have always had a soft spot in my heart for them. They are really nice cars. I kind of wish he didnt spin so bad out of the hole so it would have been a closer race but a win is a win I guess. <br>Oh yea I also ran a new best time tonight. My best time before tonight was a 14.487 and tonight I ran a 14.404. Darnit just .005 from hitting a 14.399. Oh well perhaps next time. Oh yea I ran a new best 1/8 mile time too. My previous best was a 9.117 and tonight I ran a 9.058. Darnit just .059 from hitting a 8.999. Oh well maybe next time. I now need to update my sig again.<p>Perhaps 1.6 rockers will get me there but a 100 shot will get me there for sure and probably into the 13's with a 100 shot as well. However I think I am not going to go with a 100 unless I get a progressive controller so i can feather in the nitrous to make it easier on the engine. I plan to be low 13's by summer of 2000. Oh Yea Baby(best austim powers imitation)<br>------------------<br>The Car: <br>85 Pontiac Fiero GT<br>Drivetrain:<br>2.8 V6 3.08 FD 3 spd auto <br>MODS:<br>Crane HI-6S ignition <br>PS-91 Coil<br>Accel 8.8 mm wires<br>Throttle Body bypass<br>K&N air filter<br>Ported exhaust manifolds<br>Underdrive Pulley<br>NOS 70 hp shot<br>FUTURE MODS: <br>Hi lift cam full port and polish of heads and intake, shift kit, 2.5 cat-back with flowmaster muffler<br>Best e.t. to date: <br>R/T:.745<br>60': 1.958 <br>330': 5.827<br>1/8: 9.11 MPH: 74.26<br>990': 11.92<br>1/4: 14.487 MPH: 89.84 <IMG SRC="/ubb/redface.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15>(<br>My fastest E.T but slowest MPH. Whats up with that?<br>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||09-04-99||05:21 PM||||GOOD KILL Shaun!! The GN's were built from 84-87. The 84-85 GN's were NOT inter-cooled and had machined, spoked wheels. (I smoked an 85 model on the street). The 86-87 GN's were inter-cooled and had chrome plated wheels. That is the easiest way to tell them apart, by the wheels.
Z||000002||Phantom Rage||09-04-99||07:06 PM||||  I think your time, seems to relate a bit more with you initial take off, and your speed due more to how fast your car accelerates through the 1/4.  Of coarse everything is interrelated.<br>  Just something I noticed at the 1st annual Florida Import Challenge (Gainesville).  <p>
